      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The nametag mod did an excellent job at this where by default when enabling this, at 3m the nametag was visible, and at 2m the nametag was not. This was easily one of my favorite features. If I needed to know who someone was while up close, I'd just open my menu and it would appear. Having this option and even allowing us to vary the distances at which nametags begin to fade in/out would be incredible. Please hear this VRChat. This was amazing for mirror dwellers. I don't want my only option to be disabling them altogether like it's all or nothing.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-04-23T11:56:42.188Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Instead turn on/off nametags, we should do something about nametags....\n\nProblem 1: Small avatars.\nIf you walk to someone with small avatar, the nametag will also at lower position, caused the nametag is at same eye height for normal size avatars. It will block your view pretty much and that is annoying.\n\nProblem 2: big distance. The nametags are even showed at big distance, but you cannot read name at all, perhaps slight color. Pretty useless.\n\nSo fade in/out should good idea for nametags. It will not show nametags at big distance and will even off. (saves fps a little) and at some distance when player comes in readable distance, the nametags will fade in slowly to visible nametag.\n\nAnd when they walked very near you, it should fade out so the nametag will not block your view.\nVery useful when sitting together by the mirror.",
